     "body": "The participant paradigms that contextualize this analysis. An analysis can span paradigms, as a cross-task conjunction or a localizer-plus-main-task analysis does.\nA resting-state analysis names its Task here like any other: the resting-state protocol is a paradigm, and a Task record exists for it. What leaves this empty is an analysis with no paradigm at all -- morphometry, diffusion, a static PET scan -- which is linked through `acquisitions` instead."
